# Line endings are LF, everywhere, on every platform. `text=auto` lets git
# decide what is text; `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending so a checkout on
# Windows cannot hand a tool a CRLF file to half-convert. Without this line a
# single edit that writes CRLF into an LF file produces a MIXED file, which is
# the state that actually costs time: it defeats diffs and hides real changes
# inside whitespace churn.
* text=auto eol=lf
